{"name":"Meadow Lane","hex":"#c0d7cd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"meadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A field or pasture; a piece of land either intentionally cultivated with grass or (especially) naturally covered with grass, especially one that is intended to be mown for hay or to be grazed.","Low land covered with coarse grass or rank herbage near rivers and in marshy places by the sea."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cultivate with grass in order to produce hay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meadow"},{"term":"lane","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A road, street, or similar thoroughfare.","A narrow passageway between fences, walls, hedges or trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meadow Lane","blocks":[{"text":"Meadow Lane is a football stadium in Nottingham, England. It is the home ground of Notts County, who have played there since it opened in 1910. The stadium was also home to Notts County Ladies F.C. from 2014 to 2017."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Nottingham_county_fc_notts_stadium.jpg/330px-Nottingham_county_fc_notts_stadium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadow_Lane","wikidata":"Q1192396"},{"title":"Meadow","blocks":[{"text":"A meadow is an open habitat or field, vegetated by grasses, herbs, and other non-woody plants. Trees or shrubs may sparsely populate meadows, as long as they maintain an open character. Meadows can occur naturally under favourable conditions but are often artificially created from cleared shrub or woodland for the production of hay, fodder or livestock. Meadow habitats as a group are characterized as semi-natural grasslands, meaning that they are largely composed of species native to the region, with only limited human intervention."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Blumenwiese_bei_Obermaiselstein05.jpg/330px-Blumenwiese_bei_Obermaiselstein05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadow","wikidata":"Q7777019"},{"title":"Lane","blocks":[{"text":"In road transport, a lane is part of a roadway that is designated to be used by a single line of vehicles to control and guide drivers and reduce traffic conflicts. Most public roads (highways) have at least two lanes, one for traffic in each direction, generally separated by lane markings. On multilane roadways and busier two-lane roads, lanes are generally designated with road surface markings. Major highways often have two multi-lane roadways separated by a median."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Montague_Expressway.jpg/330px-Montague_Expressway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lane","wikidata":"Q3222002"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/MeadowLane2.jpg/500px-MeadowLane2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/MeadowLane2.jpg/500px-MeadowLane2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Jimmy Sirrel Stand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeadowLane2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/MeadowLane3.jpg/500px-MeadowLane3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/MeadowLane3.jpg/500px-MeadowLane3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Derek Pavis Stand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeadowLane3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/MeadowLane1.jpg/500px-Meado